1
00:00:01,921 --> 00:00:03,298
Hoo, hoo!

2
00:00:03,410 --> 00:00:04,337
Hi!

3
00:00:04,387 --> 00:00:06,414
It's me, Popcorn!

4
00:00:06,536 --> 00:00:11,767
Welcome to Popcorn Tales, the
cozy nest of bedtime stories.

5
00:00:12,079 --> 00:00:15,526
Hug your teddy, because
tonight's story is:

6
00:00:15,576 --> 00:00:18,333
Snow White and the Seven Dwarfs!

7
00:00:22,929 --> 00:00:28,573
Once upon a time, in a faraway kingdom,
there was a stone castle covered in

8
00:00:28,623 --> 00:00:30,343
soft white snow.

9
00:00:30,989 --> 00:00:36,550
By the window, a kind queen was sewing
slowly, watching the snowflakes fall

10
00:00:36,600 --> 00:00:37,800
over the garden.

11
00:00:38,437 --> 00:00:42,165
How I wish for a little daughter
with skin as white as snow,

12
00:00:42,215 --> 00:00:46,167
cheeks as red as roses, and
hair as black as ebony wood,

13
00:00:46,217 --> 00:00:49,672
the kind queen said, smiling at the sky.

14
00:00:50,323 --> 00:00:55,176
And her wish came true, because
soon a lovely baby girl was born,

15
00:00:55,226 --> 00:00:58,265
and everyone began to call her Snow White.

16
00:00:58,893 --> 00:01:02,557
The years went by, and the
king married a new queen,

17
00:01:02,685 --> 00:01:06,432
who was very elegant but also very vain.

18
00:01:07,072 --> 00:01:10,745
This new queen had a magic
mirror hanging on the wall,

19
00:01:10,795 --> 00:01:13,056
and it always told the truth.

20
00:01:16,620 --> 00:01:21,677
Mirror, little mirror on the wall, who
is the fairest in this whole kingdom?

21
00:01:21,727 --> 00:01:25,210
the Queen asked, straightening
her golden crown.

22
00:01:25,802 --> 00:01:30,724
You are very beautiful, my queen, but
Snow White has a lovely face and an even

23
00:01:30,774 --> 00:01:31,960
kinder heart,

24
00:01:32,010 --> 00:01:36,508
the magic mirror answered in
its calm and gentle voice.

25
00:01:37,570 --> 00:01:42,590
The queen's heart filled with envy,
and the envy made her face grumpier and

26
00:01:42,640 --> 00:01:43,840
grumpier.

27
00:01:44,318 --> 00:01:48,246
So she ordered a huntsman
to take Snow White far away,

28
00:01:48,360 --> 00:01:50,010
deep into the forest.

29
00:01:50,628 --> 00:01:55,314
But the huntsman was a gentle man,
and he could not bring himself to do

30
00:01:55,364 --> 00:01:58,347
anything unkind to the princess.

31
00:01:59,037 --> 00:02:03,701
He pointed to a leafy path and asked
the girl to run to a safe place,

32
00:02:03,774 --> 00:02:05,687
far away from the castle.

33
00:02:06,310 --> 00:02:10,801
The forest grew darker, and the wind
began to whistle through the long

34
00:02:10,851 --> 00:02:12,051
branches.

35
00:02:12,195 --> 00:02:17,798
Snow White felt a tiny bit afraid, but
soon she saw two shiny little eyes on a

36
00:02:17,848 --> 00:02:19,123
low branch.

37
00:02:19,725 --> 00:02:21,101
Hoo, hoo!

38
00:02:21,210 --> 00:02:26,719
Don't be afraid, princess, I am
Popcorn, and I know a safe little place

39
00:02:26,769 --> 00:02:27,690
nearby,

40
00:02:27,740 --> 00:02:31,377
Popcorn said, opening her little wings.

41
00:02:32,004 --> 00:02:36,870
Snow White smiled with relief and
followed the little owl along the moonlit

42
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:38,120
path.

43
00:02:41,188 --> 00:02:45,777
At the end of the path, there was a
little wooden cottage with an open door

44
00:02:45,827 --> 00:02:48,269
and a tiny light in the window.

45
00:02:48,922 --> 00:02:53,302
Inside, the table was set with seven
little plates, seven little cups,

46
00:02:53,352 --> 00:02:55,863
and seven very small spoons.

47
00:02:56,481 --> 00:03:01,658
Snow White was so hungry that she ate
just a tiny bit from each little plate,

48
00:03:01,731 --> 00:03:03,714
so nobody would go without.

49
00:03:04,328 --> 00:03:08,978
Then she saw seven little beds in
a row, lay down on the last one,

50
00:03:09,036 --> 00:03:11,381
and fell into a deep sleep.

51
00:03:18,048 --> 00:03:22,011
When night came, the owners of the
cottage returned from their work in the

52
00:03:22,061 --> 00:03:25,656
mountains, where they
dug for precious stones.

53
00:03:26,280 --> 00:03:32,485
They were seven small, bearded dwarfs,
each one holding a glowing lantern.

54
00:03:35,812 --> 00:03:39,543
Somebody ate a little from my plate
and fell asleep in my little bed!

55
00:03:39,593 --> 00:03:43,382
the youngest dwarf whispered,
holding up his lantern.

56
00:03:44,032 --> 00:03:48,362
The seven of them tiptoed closer,
saw the princess sleeping,

57
00:03:48,434 --> 00:03:50,709
and let her rest until the morning.

58
00:03:51,796 --> 00:03:56,204
In the morning, Snow White woke up and
told the dwarfs everything that had

59
00:03:56,254 --> 00:03:57,454
happened.

60
00:03:59,794 --> 00:04:03,702
You can live here with us, and we will
take care of you like a little sister,

61
00:04:03,752 --> 00:04:06,916
the oldest dwarf said with a kind smile.

62
00:04:07,596 --> 00:04:11,773
From that day on, the princess
helped look after the cottage,

63
00:04:11,832 --> 00:04:15,426
and Popcorn came to visit
her every afternoon.

64
00:04:16,068 --> 00:04:20,949
Every morning, before leaving for the
mountains, the oldest dwarf repeated the

65
00:04:20,999 --> 00:04:22,482
same advice.

66
00:04:23,120 --> 00:04:27,470
Please be very careful, dear princess,
and never open the door to people you

67
00:04:27,520 --> 00:04:28,528
do not know,

68
00:04:28,578 --> 00:04:32,298
the oldest dwarf warned, very seriously.

69
00:04:33,409 --> 00:04:38,109
Back at the castle, the queen asked the
mirror once more who was the fairest

70
00:04:38,159 --> 00:04:39,359
of them all.

71
00:04:42,616 --> 00:04:46,486
Snow White lives with the seven
dwarfs, beyond the mountains,

72
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:48,816
and she is still the fairest of them all,

73
00:04:48,866 --> 00:04:53,364
the magic mirror answered in
its calm and gentle voice.

74
00:04:53,977 --> 00:04:58,357
The queen disguised herself as an old
fruit seller and filled a basket with

75
00:04:58,407 --> 00:05:00,238
shiny red apples.

76
00:05:00,866 --> 00:05:05,761
One of the apples was enchanted, and
whoever bit its red side would fall into

77
00:05:05,811 --> 00:05:08,669
a very deep enchanted sleep.

78
00:05:09,326 --> 00:05:14,392
When she reached the cottage, the old
woman knocked slowly on the wooden door.

79
00:05:16,118 --> 00:05:20,186
I cannot open the door for anyone,
because I promised my friends I would be

80
00:05:20,236 --> 00:05:21,332
careful,

81
00:05:21,382 --> 00:05:24,185
Snow White said through the little window.

82
00:05:24,792 --> 00:05:28,812
You don't need to open the door, my
dear, I only want to give you this

83
00:05:28,862 --> 00:05:30,954
beautiful apple as a present,

84
00:05:31,004 --> 00:05:34,668
the disguised Queen said
in a very sweet voice.

85
00:05:35,326 --> 00:05:40,151
The apple looked so pretty and smelled
so sweet that Snow White accepted the

86
00:05:40,201 --> 00:05:41,670
gift through the window.

87
00:05:42,323 --> 00:05:47,189
She took a tiny bite of the red
side, slowly closed her eyes,

88
00:05:47,239 --> 00:05:49,903
and fell into an enchanted sleep.

89
00:05:50,999 --> 00:05:56,574
In the evening, the seven dwarfs came
home and found the princess asleep,

90
00:05:56,624 --> 00:05:58,483
and she would not wake up.

91
00:05:59,127 --> 00:06:04,021
She looked as if she were only dreaming,
with her cheeks still as rosy as the

92
00:06:04,071 --> 00:06:05,693
roses in the garden.

93
00:06:06,332 --> 00:06:11,310
The dwarfs were very sad, but they decided
to look after her with all the love

94
00:06:11,360 --> 00:06:12,560
in the world.

95
00:06:13,081 --> 00:06:17,189
They built a clear glass case
and laid Snow White inside it,

96
00:06:17,331 --> 00:06:19,453
on a bed of soft flowers.

97
00:06:20,089 --> 00:06:24,900
Then they carried the case to a flowery
hill, and there was always one dwarf

98
00:06:24,950 --> 00:06:27,434
nearby, watching over her.

99
00:06:34,012 --> 00:06:35,389
Hoo, hoo!

100
00:06:35,490 --> 00:06:40,075
I will keep watch every night
too, until our princess wakes up,

101
00:06:40,125 --> 00:06:43,483
Popcorn promised, landing on the glass.

102
00:06:44,568 --> 00:06:50,691
A long time later, on a sunny day, a
prince rode past the hill on his horse.

103
00:06:53,622 --> 00:06:58,100
He saw the princess sleeping in the
glass case and asked the dwarfs if he

104
00:06:58,150 --> 00:07:01,619
could take her to his castle,
where she would be safe.

105
00:07:02,276 --> 00:07:07,726
The dwarfs agreed, lifted the case very
carefully, and began to walk slowly

106
00:07:07,776 --> 00:07:08,976
down the hill.

107
00:07:09,558 --> 00:07:13,500
Suddenly, one of the dwarfs
tripped over a hidden root,

108
00:07:13,572 --> 00:07:16,264
and the glass case gently swayed.

109
00:07:16,935 --> 00:07:21,982
With that little bump, the tiny piece
of enchanted apple came out of the

110
00:07:22,032 --> 00:07:25,432
princess's mouth, and
the spell was broken!

111
00:07:29,012 --> 00:07:33,975
Snow White opened her eyes, stretched
her arms, and looked around in great

112
00:07:34,025 --> 00:07:35,245
surprise.

113
00:07:35,867 --> 00:07:39,293
Oh my, where in the world am I right now?

114
00:07:39,504 --> 00:07:43,176
What a joy to see all my
friends right here beside me!

115
00:07:43,226 --> 00:07:45,695
Snow White said with a smile.

116
00:07:46,759 --> 00:07:51,625
Back at the old castle, the magic mirror
told the queen that Snow White was

117
00:07:51,675 --> 00:07:53,450
awake and happy.

118
00:07:54,097 --> 00:07:57,733
The queen understood that envy
would never make her happy,

119
00:07:57,792 --> 00:08:02,150
so she went far, far
away and never came back.

120
00:08:02,792 --> 00:08:06,700
The prince and Snow White had
a wedding party full of music,

121
00:08:06,750 --> 00:08:08,414
flowers, and cake.

122
00:08:09,058 --> 00:08:13,342
The seven dwarfs were the guests of
honor, and they danced with the princess

123
00:08:13,392 --> 00:08:14,917
all night long.

124
00:08:15,570 --> 00:08:20,381
Popcorn landed on the window of the
great hall, straightened her red bow,

125
00:08:20,431 --> 00:08:23,303
and spoke in a sweet little voice.

126
00:08:23,890 --> 00:08:25,267
Hoo, hoo!

127
00:08:25,383 --> 00:08:30,850
True beauty lives in a kind heart, and
good friends always take care of us,

128
00:08:30,900 --> 00:08:34,300
Popcorn said in her soft and sweet voice.

129
00:08:34,946 --> 00:08:40,187
And Snow White lived happily ever after,
always close to her friends from the

130
00:08:40,237 --> 00:08:41,437
forest.

131
00:08:48,622 --> 00:08:49,822
The End.

132
00:08:51,529 --> 00:08:52,241
Hoo...

133
00:08:52,291 --> 00:08:53,316
Psst!

134
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:54,938
Are you still awake?

135
00:08:55,092 --> 00:08:57,145
Did you like tonight's story?

136
00:08:57,294 --> 00:09:02,270
Snow White and Popcorn showed us that
true beauty lives in a kind heart,

137
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:05,610
and that good friends
always take care of us.

138
00:09:05,909 --> 00:09:10,215
Good night, sleep tight, and
have the sweetest dreams.

139
00:09:10,511 --> 00:09:15,409
Grown-ups: if you enjoyed it,
please subscribe to Popcorn Tales,

140
00:09:15,459 --> 00:09:17,864
for more stories at bedtime.

141
00:09:18,168 --> 00:09:19,368
Hoo...

